<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Different actions do different jobs</h2>
      <p><b>Sort each action by its real job.</b> Similar words do not always mean the same solution.</p>
      <grid padding-top="42pt" spacing="medium" marker-straddle="true" marker-align="center" marker-position="above" marker-shape="circle" marker-style="solid" marker-size="large" marker="icon">
        <grid-item colspan="20" background-color="palette-3">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="international agreement protecting atmosphere"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h3>Ozone recovery</h3>
          <p>Countries phase out ozone-depleting substances. Trained adults safely service old cooling equipment.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="sun hat shade and sunscreen"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h3>Sun safety</h3>
          <p>Shade, clothing and sunscreen protect skin from UV now.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="thermometer beside cooling unit"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h3>Climate</h3>
          <p>HFCs do not deplete ozone, but many can warm the climate.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>